				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				727,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(desktop): enhance Wind workbench with comprehensive Tauri integration and robust error handling\n\nThis commit significantly enhances the Wind desktop application with comprehensive Tauri integration, advanced error handling, and defensive coding patterns throughout the codebase. The changes transform the application from a basic VSCode workbench implementation to a production-ready desktop application with robust error recovery and graceful degradation capabilities.\n\nKey improvements include:\n\n**Enhanced DesktopMain Implementation:**\n- Added comprehensive VSCode service wrapping with defensive coding patterns\n- Implemented enhanced instantiation service bridge with service caching and error handling\n- Created robust workbench instantiation with connection health monitoring\n- Added graceful degradation patterns with fallback UI for critical errors\n- Improved logging and error tracking throughout the startup sequence\n\n**Tauri Integration Support:**\n- Updated ESBuild configuration with proper Tauri webview targeting\n- Added external dependencies for Tauri APIs (@tauri-apps/api)\n- Enhanced path mapping for VSCode modules and Tauri integration\n- Added asset processing optimized for Tauri deployment\n- Implemented build cleaning for target directories\n\n**Configuration Enhancements:**\n- Added comprehensive TypeScript configuration (tsconfig.json) with modern ES2022 target\n- Implemented path mapping for VSCode modules and external dependencies\n- Added proper module resolution for ES modules and Tauri integration\n- Enhanced build options with source map generation and optimization\n\n**Security Documentation Update:**\n- Updated SECURITY.md to reflect current filesystem handlers (removed outdated references to River and Sun)\n\n**Infrastructure Improvements:**\n- Added Bridge.ts file (non-UTF-8 content) for enhanced IPC communication\n- Enhanced IPC service definition with Tauri integration support and connection state management\n\nThese changes ensure the Wind workbench can operate reliably in production environments with comprehensive error recovery, proper Tauri integration, and enhanced developer experience through improved build tooling and configuration.",
			"SHA": "6eb3668cda707a7be920073844084a27586d65d2"
		}
